= Validate =

#type: node
#context: sop
#internal: a3ob_validate
#tags: arma, p3d

"""Checks a P3D geometry or a LOD geometry the way the export does and shows what is wrong. Changes nothing."""

Run this node before you export. It looks for problems that Arma would reject or that break the model, and lists them as messages on the node. It does not change the geometry.

@inputs

P3D geometry or LOD geometry:
    The model to check: a whole P3D from Assemble LODs, or a single LOD.

@parameters

== Error Checking == (tab_checking)

These parameters are in the Error Checking tab.

Errors Show As:
    #id: errorlevel

    Type: Menu. Default: Error (stop here).

    Error (stop here):
        The node turns red and the nodes below it stop.

    Warning (keep geometry):
        The node turns yellow and the geometry keeps flowing; the text still starts with Error:. Saving stops on errors either way.

Warnings Count As Errors:
    #id: strict

    Treat every warning as an error. Off by default: a warning can be what you meant.

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

Duplicate LODs:
    #id: dupes

    What to do with a LOD whose type and resolution were already written: Fail, Skip the later one, or Ignore and write both.

    Type: Menu. Default: Fail.

    Choices: Fail, Skip, Ignore.

Max Messages:
    #id: maxmessages

    How many messages the node shows. The rest are counted in one line and listed in the console.

    Type: Whole number. Default: 25. Allowed: At least 1; no upper limit.

== LOD Rules == (tab_rules)

These parameters are in the LOD Rules tab.

Check LOD-Type Rules:
    #id: typerules

    Warn about what Object Builder's validator would: rules for geometry, shadow, roadway and other LOD types. Each rule has its own switch below.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

At most 2 UV sets:
    #id: t2uv2

    The LOD has no more than 2 UV sets. (Rule T2-UV2.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Contiguous mesh:
    #id: t2contig

    Geometry, shadow and underground LODs: no flipped polygons (shared edges run in opposite directions). (Rule T2-CONTIG.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Triangulated:
    #id: t2tri

    Underground LODs: every polygon is a triangle. Geometry and shadow LODs: triangles and convex quads. (Rule T2-TRI.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Convex mesh:
    #id: t2convex

    Geometry and underground LODs: every shared edge is convex or flat. (Rule T2-CONVEX.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Component selections:
    #id: t2comp

    Geometry and underground LODs: a group called component01, component02, ... exists. (Rule T2-COMP.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Mass is set:
    #id: t2mass

    Geometry LOD: a note (not a warning) when the points have a total mass below 0.001. (Rule T2-MASS.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Every point has mass:
    #id: t2massall

    Geometry LOD: every point has a mass of at least 0.001. (Rule T2-MASSALL.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

No smooth edges:
    #id: t2sharp

    Shadow and underground LODs: with smooth polygons, every shared edge is in a3ob_sharp. (Rule T2-SHARP.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

No materials:
    #id: t2nomat

    Underground LODs: no polygon has a texture or material. Shadow LODs may have them. (Rule T2-NOMAT.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Conventional shadow resolution:
    #id: t2shadowres

    Shadow LODs: the resolution is 0, 10, 1000, 1010 or 1020. Off by default. (Rule T2-SHADOWRES.)

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

Shadow not disabled:
    #id: t2shadowoff

    Shadow LODs: no LODNoShadow = 1 property. Off by default. (Rule T2-SHADOWOFF.)

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

No edges in point clouds:
    #id: t2pcedge

    Memory, land contact and hit-point LODs: no 2-point primitives. (Rule T2-PC-EDGE.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

No faces in point clouds:
    #id: t2pcface

    Memory, land contact and hit-point LODs: no polygons. (Rule T2-PC-FACE.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Has polygons:
    #id: t2rwfaces

    Roadway, ground layer and paths LODs: at least one polygon. (Rule T2-RW-FACES.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Roadway point limit:
    #id: t2rwlimit

    Roadway LODs: at most 255 points. (Rule T2-RW-LIMIT.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Roadway sound textures:
    #id: t2rwsound

    Roadway LODs: every polygon has a texture (the sound). (Rule T2-RW-SOUND.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Ground layer UV set:
    #id: t2gluv

    Ground layer LODs: exactly one UV set. (Rule T2-GL-UV.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Ground layer UV values:
    #id: t2gluvvalues

    Ground layer LODs: every UV is (0, 0), (1, 0), (1, 1) or (1, -1). (Rule T2-GL-UVVALUES.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Path entry points:
    #id: t2pathentry

    Paths LODs: a group called in01, in02, ... exists. (Rule T2-PATH-ENTRY.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Path position points:
    #id: t2pathpos

    Paths LODs: the same test as the entry rule (as in Object Builder, which tests entry points twice). (Rule T2-PATH-POS.)

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

The full page for this node is docs/user/reference/a3ob_validate.html in the A3OB folder. Open it in a web browser.
